WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.010
The pipeline begins by taking a single RGB image of an indoor room as input.

2
00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:10.900
A convolutional backbone network processes the image to extract shared feature representations.

3
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:13.940
The top convolutional branch targets surface structure.

4
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:18.470
It predicts the individual spatial planes that compose the room layout.

5
00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:21.510
The middle convolutional branch processes structural boundaries.

6
00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:25.290
It detects the vertical lines located between adjacent walls.

7
00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:28.710
The bottom convolutional branch focuses on spatial orientation.

8
00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:32.490
It estimates dense three-dimensional parameters for each identified plane.

9
00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:37.380
A geometric reasoning module then integrates the predicted planes, lines, and parameters.

10
00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:40.430
This module generates the final reconstruction results.

11
00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:44.210
Producing a two-dimensional semantic segmentation of the room surfaces.

12
00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:47.620
And a geometrically consistent three-dimensional room layout model.

